6. Certificate Contract

The certificate is

\pi_t = \langle m,\; p_{\mathrm{id}},\; p_{\mathrm{hash}},\; a,\; \mathcal{X}_t,\; W,\; q,\; d,\; \rho \rangle,

with fields bounded as in Table 1.

Table 1 — Certificate fields and bounds

Field Representation Bound
m u32 model id must match registry
p_{\mathrm{id}} u32 policy version strictly monotonic
p_{\mathrm{hash}} 32-byte hash must match trusted store
a opaque action bytes \le 512 B
\mathcal{X}_t canonical zonotope (c,G) n \le 12, m \le 32
W interval box entry-wise bounded
q u64 sequence number strictly increasing
d u64 deadline d > \mathrm{now} + \Delta_{\mathrm{WCET}}
\rho type-tagged proof object \le 16 KiB

The monitor rejects certificates exceeding these bounds at the framing layer, before parsing \rho. Proof size is a denial-of-service surface and must be bounded before it is trusted.

Acceptance. The monitor authorizes a_t only if

\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{Accept}(\pi_t) \iff{}& \mathrm{WellFormed}(\pi_t) \land \mathrm{Fresh}(\pi_t) \land \mathrm{PolicyMatch}(\pi_t) \\
& \land \mathrm{ProofCheck}(\rho) \land \mathrm{RobustSafe}(a_t, \mathcal{X}_t, W) \\
& \land \mathrm{DeadlineValid}(\pi_t) \land F(\mathcal{X}_t, a_t, W) \subseteq K \\
& \land \bigwedge_{i} \mu_i(\mathcal{X}_t) \ge 0 \land \|\epsilon(y_t)\| \le \epsilon_{\max}(\hat{x}_t).
\end{aligned}

