7. Two Certificate Modes

7.1 Mode L — containment witness on the linear plant

For x^{+} = Ax + Bu + w, the successor of (c,G) is (Ac + Bu,\; [AG,\; I]). On this plant the monitor can recompute the successor cheaply, so the certificate does not offload computation. Its role is replay safety: it binds the agent's proposal to a specific (c,G) so that the monitor's recomputation is tied to the exact invocation. Containment in the polytope K is checked by the support-function inequalities

h_i^{\top} c + \| G^{\top} h_i \|_1 \le b_i \quad \forall i.

This is a linear sufficient condition for containment, not an exact test. Exact zonotope containment is co-NP-complete in general, with exact polynomial algorithms only when dimension or generator count is fixed. The sufficient condition is sound and incomplete; its conservatism is reported.

7.2 Mode N — measurement-robust barrier certificate on the nonlinear plant

On a nonlinear plant the successor set is not a zonotope and exact containment is unavailable. The certificate carries a barrier witness

\rho_{\mathrm{bar}} = \langle h,\; k_B,\; L_f,\; L_h,\; L_{\mathcal{L}_f h},\; \epsilon(y),\; \text{Farkas} \rangle.

The Lipschitz constants, the barrier function, the backup controller, and the error bound come from the trusted registry and sensor provenance, never from the agent's certificate. The monitor verifies the tightened condition

b_i(\hat{x}) - \mu(\epsilon, L) \ge 0, \qquad \mu = \left( L_{\mathcal{L}_f h} + L_h \|k_B\| \right) \epsilon,

not the nominal condition b_i(\hat{x}) \ge 0. Without \mu, the condition can hold for the true state and fail for the estimate—the known fragility of non-robust barrier checking. A linearisation of the dynamics requires a bounded remainder term; that term is part of the registry data, not the certificate.

Farkas semantics, corrected. The v0.3 draft stated that the Farkas witness proves the constraints “feasible.” This is a category error. Farkas' lemma proves that a linear implication holds—that one inequality is implied by others, or that a set is infeasible. The correct statement is: the witness proves that the tightened constraint is implied by the linearised dynamics and barrier conditions, or that its negation is infeasible.

