10. Common-Cause Analysis and Coverage

Separation of components does not imply independence. ASTM F3269-21 requires RTA system coverage, and coverage collapses when a shared resource is lost. Each deployment produces a fault table of the form

Table 2 — Common-cause fault table (schema)

Resource Monitor uses Fallback uses Status Coverage impact if lost
IMU bus A bus B INDEPENDENT —
Power rail A rail B INDEPENDENT —
Processor core 0 (TT) core 1 (TT) CONDITIONALLY INDEPENDENT bounded by memory-bus WCET analysis
Communication hardware mailbox direct PWM INDEPENDENT —
Clock monitor clock watchdog clock INDEPENDENT —
Memory monitor SRAM fallback SRAM SHARED fallback claim downgraded

Where a resource is SHARED, the fallback claim is recorded as “feasible conditional on the shared resource remaining operational,” and mitigation declares loss of the nominal guarantee. No unconditional fallback claim is accepted where any dependency is SHARED.

