h = 2^{-s-1} fixed-point half-ulp
\gamma_s(x) exact concretisation of integer x
\gamma_s^{\oplus}(x) enlarged concretisation, half-width 2^{-s}
\sigma_t^{(i)} per-direction envelope slack
\epsilon_{\max} scalar measurement-error budget

A.2 Convention on "safe"

The word safe never appears in this document as an unqualified predicate on a system. It appears only as (i) a membership test x \in S_{\mathrm{safe}} for a set declared in the model, (ii) an obligation name, or (iii) a claim explicitly withdrawn. A statement of the form "the system is safe" is malformed in this specification and is to be treated as a defect wherever found.

A.3 Convention on quantification over the plant

Every invariance statement is quantified over the model F. No statement in this document quantifies over the physical plant. The relation between model and plant is not proved here; it is the subject of the model-mismatch campaign of Appendix I.4, which makes no safety claim.

