Appendix G — Refinement Pipeline, Lean Statements, and TCB

G.1 Extractable subset

The monitor's decision core is written in a subset of safe Rust that the extraction toolchain can translate:

· no unsafe, no raw pointers;
· no dynamic allocation on the decision path;
· monomorphic types only (no trait objects, no closures capturing environment);
· bounded loops with compile-time-known bounds where possible;
· no external crates on the decision path;
· integer arithmetic only, with explicit checked_* or saturating operations and explicit flag propagation.

The subset is not a stylistic preference. Aeneas supports a limited fragment; unsupported constructs are reported as translation failures. Writing outside the subset produces an INCONCLUSIVE file, which blocks policy activation (G.4).

