Appendix M — Closing Statement on the Status of This Document

This monograph contains no implementation, no simulation, no machine-checked proof, and no physical test. The paper proofs of Appendices B, C, D, E, F, and H are hand arguments. They are offered because an obligation with no proof sketch is not an obligation but a wish; they are labelled [P] rather than [V] discharged because a hand argument does not survive a compiler.

The document is organised so that its value does not depend on its claims being true. Each claim is paired with a statement of what would refute it. Sixteen claims from earlier drafts have already been refuted by this analysis and are recorded in Appendix J. One reference plant is predicted to fail its central obligation and the failure is recorded in advance. The obligation ledger is deliberately unbalanced.

A safety architecture that cannot be falsified cannot be audited. The contribution claimed here is not a guarantee, but a precise account of which guarantee is being attempted, on which plant, under which assumptions, with which obligations outstanding, and with which pre-registered conditions would count as its refutation.

